{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>Like a hired worker, like a resident, he shall be with you.</b> Both are hired workers, except that a hired worker is a day laborer, and a resident is a yearly hire. And just as you may not impose on a day laborer work that is hard in his eyes — since he can withdraw immediately, for a worker may withdraw even in the middle of the day — so too a resident: you shall not work him with crushing labor, and there shall be no distinction between him and the hired worker." "<b>Until the jubilee year he shall work with you.</b> Above — ״and you shall proclaim freedom״ — it speaks of one sold by the court; here it speaks of one who sells himself on account of his poverty."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:15:24.063311789Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}